**Amendment (Compact full-content representation)** · `amend:observe:compact-content` Refines (`amend:observe:full-content`) without changing the public-content boundary. Public byte values use a tagged UTF-8 JSON string when valid, otherwise padded RFC 4648 base64, with their byte length. Available structural Debug carriers are decoded into tagged JSON constructors, fields, sequences and literals; custom formatting outside that grammar remains explicitly identified available text rather than guessed fields or an invented serialization contract. Opaque capabilities retain their declared unavailable representation. Payload children are addressed before envelopes, so changing timestamps or totals does not duplicate their stored content. A complete JSON field exceeding 65,536 encoded bytes is stored once by SHA-256 content address, with digest, original encoded length and path replacing the inline representation; existing content is verified and atomic publication never overwrites an object. The default command store is .lane/observations/objects/sha256 beneath its working directory, overridden by PN_OBSERVE_ARTIFACT_DIR; the gate explicitly selects its checkout's .lane/observations. Artifact I/O runs on the delivery worker. Complete delivered records remain below one MiB; a larger envelope is itself addressed. Queue admission is bounded by 64 records and 64 MiB of captured serialized bytes, with two reserved one-MiB summary slots, eight one-MiB diagnostic slots and one independent drain request; terminal records are serviced before ordinary backlog and queue saturation cannot reject the drain immediately; capacity, unavailable storage and disconnected delivery count whole-observation loss under (`rule:observe:sampling`), never field filtering or binding failure. The default gate keeps its observation records inline; explicit traced-run streams can be separated with ci/observation_log.py without changing their bytes. Structural value traits inherit the consuming operation so hashing, comparison, clone and teardown do not repeatedly record the same whole value.

**Amendment (Independent resource qualification)** · `amend:observe:resource-qualification` Implements the independent qualification promised by (`amend:observe:core-accounting`): resources accepts separate current and cumulative accuracy arguments. An unavailable current reading becomes null while retaining the previously observed high-water value and its accuracy; it does not claim that unobserved intervals had no higher usage. Cumulative availability is independent. The controlled witness checks mixed exact and estimated values and a later unavailable current reading without substituting zero.

**Amendment (Body-bound class decisions)** · `amend:observe:semantic-classes` Refines (`amend:observe:coverage-admission`): the operation register records seven reviewer-confirmed semantic classes, their premises and named labelled operations. Each body binds to a class decision and an item-specific premise, alongside its existing separate full-recording, secret-flow and exposure assessments. Exceptions name the class and actual enclosing operation set; const, bootstrap and observation-internal exceptions remain distinct from structural value-trait inheritance. New payload representation, resource qualification and protected configuration bodies carry their additional premises locally. Mechanical checks reject missing class decisions or enclosing operation sets and changed bodies or types; they do not turn these semantic decisions into parser proofs.

**Amendment (Current carrier authority)** · `amend:observe:carrier-authority` Updates the Python-exhibition clause of (`amend:observe:foundation-evidence`) under (`amend:testing:python-carrier-adoption`): Python claim names in the evidence paragraphs are now ordinary citations resolved by the deployed linter, while the evidence join retains site/result, scoped-premise and bidirectional obligation checks. The complete locked transitive dependency review for (`amend:observe:export-dependencies`) is (`amend:observe:transitive-review`); inactive target branches remain reviewed without being claimed as host execution evidence.

**Amendment (Emission levels)** · `amend:observe:emission-levels` Clarifies (`amend:observe:full-content`), (`rule:observe:privacy`) and (`dec:observe:sinks`): full content is an instrumentation capability, while emission and persistence follow the selected level. With PN_OBSERVE_LEVEL unset or set to default, the executable emits WARN and ERROR diagnostics, command completion metering with monotonic duration in seconds, outcome and totals, metric summaries, and a final observation-status record. Per-operation public payloads are not formatted or persisted at that level. PN_OBSERVE_LEVEL=trace enables complete compact-encoded span and operation content, including content-addressed objects under (`amend:observe:compact-content`); an unknown level is refused by name by the bootstrap. Secret roles and markers are unchanged at every level. Legacy debug and default-level arguments do not silently opt into persistence; RUST_LOG remains available to the separate directive-selection utility, not this bootstrap. Final per-process status reports successful delivery and whole-record loss before that status, excluding the status itself from delivered counts. Queue, sink and export failures never change binding results. The gate explicitly selects default, retains diagnostics inline and reports warning, error and loss counts per step. Controlled comparisons run disabled, default, trace and trace with local exporter failure against identical stdout and exit; the service-dependent remainder is unchanged.
